WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.003
- When he broke the sign in Dodger
Stadium during batting practice,

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.671
I went in. This is a playoff
game, mind you.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.005
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:08.008
- I went in, I said, "Hey, I need
some Dodger letterhead."

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:11.428
I had it typed up, "Hey, on behalf
of the Los Angeles Dodgers,

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:14.347
we are fining you $10,000 for breaking the sign."

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.306
Signed so and so.

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:18.309
And I put it on his chair, and
he looked at it, he goes,

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:21.354
"What should I do?" Now, this is
30 minutes before the first pitch.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.564
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:23.314
- "You gotta pay it."

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:24.816
- [Laughing]

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:33.158
♪♪♪

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:35.201
- [Master Tesfatsion] So who
we got in the pool hall today?

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.286
- [Curtis Granderson] What's going on man?

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:37.704
-  Curtis Granderson, what's
good with you baby?

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.372
-  Man, I'm all good. Appreciate
you having me here.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.499
- Hey man, it’s good chopping up with
you. Let’s see how you break though.

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:42.876
-  All right, let's see. 
- Let’s see how nice you are.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.960
- Let's see.

00:00:45.086 --> 00:00:46.296
All right.

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:47.547
- So where did you 
start off? High A or like-

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:51.217
- I started off in Short-Season
A in Oneonta, New York.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:55.055
Small town. I remember my scout
that drafted me, Jerome Cochran said,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:59.809
"Man you gonna love it. It's beautiful up
there. It's a ton of trees and everything."

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:03.271
It was a lot of trees but it wasn’t
nothing else up there. Oh, man.

00:01:03.271 --> 00:01:04.981
- I mean we see it a lot in
terms of the Minor Leagues.

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:08.359
You've got people who are coming
from the Dominican. Venezuela.

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:10.570
And they're also coming through
the same ranks as you talk about.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.282
How did you assimilate with all these different
people from all these different cultures

00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:16.785
that you probably never been
open or experienced to?

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:20.663
- You know, growing up in Chicago, even
though I had Sammy Sosa playing for the Cubs

00:01:20.663 --> 00:01:22.540
or Ozzie Guillén playing for the White Sox,

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.376
this is a little- hey, don't get mad at me
Sammy. Don't get mad at me Ozzie.

00:01:25.376 --> 00:01:27.253
I thought they were Black, right?

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.798
They look like me, they 
were playing baseball.

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:33.343
I thought Sammy Sosa was Black. I had never
seen no one with the last name Sosa before.

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:35.053
I just thought it was a different last name.

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:38.848
When I joined my team the first time,
I remember getting on the bus

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:41.351
and I said man, this is the most
Black players I ever played with.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:45.605
Now remember again, I'm coming from thinking
Ozzie is Black, thinking Sammy is Black.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.525
So I see everyone that looked
like me and I go, “What's going on?

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:51.277
How you doing? You know. Hello, hello.
How's everybody doing? What's going on?”

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.821
And no one's saying anything.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:56.783
So now I get in the back of the bus, the
bus starts going, the music starts playing.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:01.746
Now I start hearing the Latin music. I go,
“Oh. Latin, Dominican, Venezuelan.”

00:02:01.746 --> 00:02:05.917
And I realize that although we look very
similar, we're still slightly different.

00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:08.253
And then that started that process of understanding

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:13.258
OK, there's a whole different world out
there besides Chicago where I grew up 

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:15.385
and I wanted to learn it. I wanted to take it in.

00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:18.471
And I was excited to get a chance to
be on that team to start my career. 

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:20.557
[Balls hitting, ball dropping into pocket]

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:21.099
- There we go.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:24.310
- So I've been in clubhouses before.
I've covered baseball teams.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.105
And it's always been interesting
to me being in a clubhouse,

00:02:27.105 --> 00:02:30.108
knowing that there's probably going
to be two leaders in a clubhouse.

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:32.152
One of them, who's a leader
for the Latin players.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:32.902
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:34.946
- And the other one who's like
the English speaking leader.

00:02:34.946 --> 00:02:35.572
- Yup.

00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:37.699
- And most of the time, let's be
honest, it's probably a white dude.

00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:38.491
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.952
- As a Black man, how did
you fit in this dynamic

00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:42.871
when you're trying to
figure out where you fit in?

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:45.582
- As a Black man in a baseball
team, we were the minority.

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:49.586
So I think that helped us kind of be
right in the middle of both sides.

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:52.338
And I think both of them knew, "OK, cool."

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.800
We're here for you if you need us.
We’re here for you if you need us.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.137
You need us to translate and, and bring it over
here to make you feel a little more comfortable?

00:02:59.137 --> 00:02:59.971
We can do that.

00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:02.348
"How come they playing the music
so loud?" "We like it loud too.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.101
OK, you want me to tell them turn it down?
I'll tell them to turn it down a little bit."

00:03:05.101 --> 00:03:08.438
"OK, why they always listening
to country and cowboy boots?"

00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:09.856
- Man, they love some country music, bro.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:10.982
- "Man, that's what they
like too," you know?

00:03:10.982 --> 00:03:13.359
And then here we go, I got
Yoenis Céspedes. Man.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:16.779
He probably the country-est Latin Cuban dude.

00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:18.114
- [Laughing]

00:03:18.114 --> 00:03:20.241
He rode to the stadium on a horse.

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:24.120
On a horse! Not a car.
Not a bike. On a horse.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.790
This dude rode a horse. And so,
man buckles so big. And man.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.043
- But still got them neon
yellow sleeves on, like…

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.921
- So imagine that. Neon yellow sleeve,

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:36.132
hit home runs, and ride a
horse at the same- man.

00:03:36.132 --> 00:03:39.344
So, if this dude wasn't fitting in with everybody, who else could?  

00:03:39.344 --> 00:03:40.386
- [Laughing]

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.722
- My shot here? Let’s see.
Where we at? Where we at?

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.723
- I think you got it.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.391
- Oh man, it’s gonna be a tight one.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.602
- There you go. There
you go. That’s going in.

00:03:47.602 --> 00:03:48.853
- Get legs.

00:03:48.853 --> 00:03:49.270
- Oh!

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:49.854
- There we go. There we go.

00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:53.233
- You talked a lot about clubhouse
camaraderie and clubhouse chemistry.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.109
How was that one, the 2015 Mets team?

00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:59.530
- So that team, I think had no standout player.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.616
Céspedes was probably the biggest one,

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:04.535
but he still was getting his wings underneath him, right?

00:04:04.535 --> 00:04:08.706
David Wright was coming off of injury.
Michael Cuddyer had just come to us,

00:04:08.706 --> 00:04:12.210
but he was for the Twins and a lot of
people didn't watch the Twins that much.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.878
We start rolling.

00:04:13.878 --> 00:04:16.631
Daniel Murphy has probably the
best playoffs I've ever seen.

00:04:16.631 --> 00:04:19.259
That's not the guy you were
trying to not let beat you, right?

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.677
- Was anyone accounting for that, or no?

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:22.762
- I don't think anyone saw that coming.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:27.558
I mean, we go into Wrigley Field and he's
hitting the balls left and right, all over the place,

00:04:27.558 --> 00:04:30.019
and then in Dodger Stadium, that first round,

00:04:30.019 --> 00:04:32.355
Duda's breaking signs in batting practice.

00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:33.273
- [Laughing]

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:37.735
And the thing about Duda is he's just
so quiet and so calm and reserved.

00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:40.363
But again, we're locker mates.
And we both bat left-handed.

00:04:40.363 --> 00:04:43.366
So we had so many things in common,
so I always messed with him.

00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:46.494
And here comes the "We Follow
Lucas Duda" Instagram page.

00:04:46.494 --> 00:04:49.622
- Tell me about that, yeah.
How'd that come together?

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.292
- He was starting to get hot that
year. I think he hit 30 home runs.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.127
And I was like, "Duda, you
got to be on social media."

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.671
"Nah, nah, nah. I don't like social
media. I don't want any of that."

00:04:56.671 --> 00:04:59.048
And we took a picture of
him and created the page.

00:04:59.048 --> 00:05:00.967
That was it. We didn't
expect anything else.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.845
And that page got to 100,000 followers like this.

00:05:03.845 --> 00:05:08.141
So now it became our whole
team was all trying to stalk him

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.643
and just catch him in different moments.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.771
When he broke the sign in Dodger
Stadium during batting practice,

00:05:13.771 --> 00:05:16.190
I went in. This is a playoff
game, mind you.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:19.152
This is just where my mind is.
I want to keep everybody loose.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:23.239
I went in, I said, "Hey, I need some
Dodger letterhead on a piece of paper."

00:05:23.239 --> 00:05:25.992
So I got Dodger letterhead, I had it typed up,

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.411
"Hey, on behalf of the Los Angeles Dodgers,

00:05:28.411 --> 00:05:31.039
we are fining you $10,000 for breaking the sign."

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:33.875
Signed so and so. And I put it on his chair,

00:05:33.875 --> 00:05:35.918
and he looked at it, he
goes, "What should I do?"

00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:38.338
Now, this is 30 minutes
before the first pitch.

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:39.547
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:39.547 --> 00:05:41.591
- "What do you think I should do with this?"

00:05:41.591 --> 00:05:42.800
“You've got to pay it.”

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.928
- [Laughing] 
- You've got to pay- Nah.

00:05:45.928 --> 00:05:48.723
And he went out there and had a
great series. Duda did a great series.

00:05:48.723 --> 00:05:50.683
We beat the Dodgers in Dodger Stadium.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:53.311
So little things like that just
to keep everybody loose.

00:05:53.311 --> 00:05:58.691
The We Follow Lucas Duda Instagram account,
all that stuff, I think, just helped play into it all.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:01.277
- And we kept going. And then
once we got to the World Series,

00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:03.404
we just came up a little bit short there.

00:06:03.404 --> 00:06:05.948
That first game, in Kansas City, we were up.

00:06:05.948 --> 00:06:09.494
Alex Gordon hits a home run to
put it into extras. I was like, "Oh."

00:06:09.494 --> 00:06:14.874
Not losing that game, but
going to New York down 0-2,

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.919
versus going to New York 1 to 1- because I
think we were going to lose the second game.

00:06:17.919 --> 00:06:19.545
They, they, they played really well.

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.214
That puts us in a different situation.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:24.258
Because everyone says Game 3 is the
turning point and we won Game 3.

00:06:24.258 --> 00:06:27.678
Then it was just playing catch-up at that
point in time and we ran out of juice.

00:06:27.678 --> 00:06:28.304
- Yeah.

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:31.766
- You know? The Citi Field, the
blue and orange, the Seven Line,

00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:34.435
the homers out of the ballpark.
We just came up a little short.

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:37.939
But I wouldn't trade anything from that season.

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:40.775
It was great because no one expected
it, and that's what you want to be.

00:06:40.775 --> 00:06:42.026
Expect the unexpected. 

00:06:42.026 --> 00:06:43.694
- For sure. I think it’s your shot, right? 

00:06:43.694 --> 00:06:45.029
- We got insurance on the place, right?

00:06:45.029 --> 00:06:46.280
We good?
- Oh, I- I think so.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.616
- OK, all right, good. Then
we might- I may try it.

00:06:48.616 --> 00:06:49.534
You know what then, let me try it then.

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:51.160
- Go ahead, yeah. Let’s see what you can do.
- Let's see. 

00:06:52.161 --> 00:06:53.996
- Oh!
- There we go. Yeah, you know?

00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:55.498
- Aye. 
- Something slight.

00:06:55.498 --> 00:07:00.920
♪♪♪

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.047
- Now Curtis, your real childhood
passion was basketball?

00:07:03.047 --> 00:07:06.092
- Man, I wanted to hoop for as long as I 
could but you can see the height just didn’t-

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:06.801
- [Laughing]

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:08.344
- It slowed down for a little bit.

00:07:08.344 --> 00:07:10.054
- Well let’s see how nice you are
on the Pop-A-Shot. Is that cool?

00:07:10.054 --> 00:07:10.555
- Let’s do it.

00:07:10.555 --> 00:07:11.556
- You got 60 seconds. Go and hit the button.

00:07:11.556 --> 00:07:12.557
[Digital beeps from game sounding]
- Come on, bring them balls out.

00:07:12.557 --> 00:07:14.183
- I’m gonna ask you questions the whole
time. It’s gonna be fast. All right, you ready?

00:07:14.183 --> 00:07:15.184
- All right. Let’s go.

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:16.602
- Who are you listening to before a game?

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:17.520
- Outkast.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.563
- Mets or Yankees?

00:07:18.563 --> 00:07:19.522
- Mets.

00:07:19.522 --> 00:07:21.065
- Hardest pitcher to hit off of?

00:07:21.065 --> 00:07:22.233
- Brad Hand.

00:07:22.233 --> 00:07:23.609
- Funniest opponent you’ve played?

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.653
- Uh, Sean Casey.

00:07:25.653 --> 00:07:26.571
- A-Rod or Jeter?

00:07:26.571 --> 00:07:27.029
- Jeter.

00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:28.823
- Favorite wrestler?

00:07:28.823 --> 00:07:30.450
- Junkyard Dog.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.034
- Best slugger in baseball?

00:07:32.034 --> 00:07:33.578
- Miguel Cabrera.

00:07:33.578 --> 00:07:35.288
